<title>SRI LANKA: Weather-Showers seen over many parts of Sri Lanka.</title>
<headline>Weather-Showers seen over many parts of Sri Lanka.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's metereological department released the following rainfall figures for 24 hours ending Wednesday morning</p>
<p>Hydro catchment areas (in mm):</p>
<p>    Bowathenna		0</p>
<p>    Canyon		    0.7</p>
<p>    Castlereigh	     0.3</p>
<p>    Kotmale		   1.0</p>
<p>    Laxapana		  3.6</p>
<p>    Moussakele		0.8</p>
<p>    Norton		    1.2</p>
<p>    Randenigala	     33.3</p>
<p>    Victoria		  32.5</p>
<p>    Samanalawewa	    0</p>
<p>    Ukuwela		   0</p>
<p>    Rantembe		  36.5</p>
<p>The department forecast morning showers along the southwestern coastal areas and thundershowers at several places in the Central, Sabaragamuwa, North Central, Uva, Western and Northwestern provinces in the evening or night.</p>
</text>
